// Type-checks scripts/ — the repo's CLI tooling — which tsconfig.json deliberately EXCLUDES.
//
// WHY THE SPLIT. `next build` runs inside a Docker context rooted at this directory
// (see Dockerfile: the build context is 09_website-app/frontend). Everything above it,
// including the repo root's `.claude/` and `andro-prime/06_marketing/`, does not exist in
// that container. But scripts/ is repo tooling BY DESIGN: it hops out to REPO_ROOT to read
// asset markdown, keywords.csv and the shared db-owned-keys.json. Those references can never
// resolve inside the build context, so type-checking scripts/ as part of the app build makes
// the production build fail on code the app does not even import.
//
// That is exactly what happened on 2026-08-02: commit 8398468 added a build-time
// `import ... from '../../../../../.claude/skills/content-status/db-owned-keys.json'` to
// content-doctor.ts. It type-checked locally, where the file is present, and broke the Coolify
// deploy, where it is outside the context. The site stayed up on the previous image; the
// pipeline was blocked.
//
// So the boundary is now explicit rather than accidental:
//   tsconfig.json          -> the APP. Everything the container builds and serves.
//   tsconfig.scripts.json  -> the TOOLING. Runs on a full checkout, may reach REPO_ROOT.
//
// Coverage is not lost, it moved: `npm run typecheck:scripts` is wired into `npm test`, so
// scripts/ is still type-checked on a machine that has the whole repo. Verify a change here
// with BOTH `npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json` and `npm run typecheck:scripts`.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "include": [
    "scripts/**/*.ts"
  ],
  "exclude": [
    "node_modules"
  ]
}
